                <pb facs="0801" n="789" sameAs="frus:frus1940v03/pg789"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">881.00/1777: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-11-07T21:00:00+01:00">November 7, 1940—9
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 7—3:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3672. My 3654, November 6, 8 p.m. An official of the Foreign Office informed me
                    today that according to secret and reliable information the Spanish were
                    impelled to take the action they did at Tangier to forestall Italian
                    occupation.</p>
                <p>While Sir Samuel Hoare has been instructed to put an official protest on record
                    with full reservation of all British rights under the international agreements
                    governing Tangier, I gather that the Foreign Office does not view the Spanish
                    action with any undue apprehension as far as the fact of occupation is
                    concerned. They dislike the high-handed way the Spaniards acted without
                    consulting this country as required by treaty commitments and as the Spaniards
                    had specifically promised to do last June when the British consented to Spanish
                    troops moving into the International Zone.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
